WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.467
-It is so good to see you,
buddy. You look fantastic.

00:00:03.467 --> 00:00:04.767
It is your --
-Thank you so much.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:06.467
-It's your first time
here in person.

00:00:06.467 --> 00:00:08.601
-Yeah. Yeah, no,
which is a huge relief.

00:00:08.601 --> 00:00:10.300
'Cause last time we did this,
I was in my living room

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:12.701
and I got torrents of abuse from
the public for my cushions.

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:14.767
-Yeah, your couch cushions,
they didn't enjoy.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.267
-They were not up to scratch.

00:00:16.267 --> 00:00:18.367
Everyone was shocked that I was
not actually British royalty.

00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.767
And it's like, "No, this is what
poor L.A. actors look like.

00:00:20.767 --> 00:00:23.167
We're dirty. We're broke.
That couch has ramen on it."

00:00:23.167 --> 00:00:25.634
That's how that works.
-That's the way it works, yeah.

00:00:25.634 --> 00:00:26.868
-Pretty much.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.367
-I know you were
just at Comic-Con.

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.067
This is your first time
at Comic-Con.

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.033
-Yep. Yep, nerd Mecca.
It was amazing.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:33.667
-Yeah.
-It was absolutely incredible.

00:00:33.667 --> 00:00:36.434
-It really is.
But you were in Hall H.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:37.767
-Yes. Which is --
-For the first time anyone

00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.634
has been there in three years
at Comic-Con.

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:41.634
-Yeah, it was the first Hall H
in three years.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.868
Everyone was super hyped,
and we were going to Hall H

00:00:43.868 --> 00:00:45.767
with "Dungeons &amp; Dragons,"
which is pretty much

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.834
the heart of all things
Comic-Con and nerd.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:50.267
-Congratulations.
Yes, congra-- By the way.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:51.801
So, you played that trailer.

00:00:51.801 --> 00:00:53.567
By the way, it has
over like 16 million hits,

00:00:53.567 --> 00:00:55.300
so congratulations on that.
-Thank you very much.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.767
-But the "Dungeons &amp; Dragons"
trailer, you premiere it.

00:00:57.767 --> 00:01:00.734
Hall H. And what do you see?
And what do they do?

00:01:00.734 --> 00:01:02.434
-You don't see a damn thing
because you black out.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:04.033
This thing's terrifying.
-It's terrifying.

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.133
-Like, I tried to ask, like,
Chris Evans and Ana de Armas

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.434
because they've
done this before.

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:08.934
I was like, "Hey.
I'm going to Hall H.

00:01:08.934 --> 00:01:10.701
You got any survival tips?
And they're like, "Oh, my God!

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:12.067
Hall H?!"
-"Ohh!"

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.601
-"No, man, that's --" And
I was like, "Yeah, thank you.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.067
Survival tips." They're like,
"Man, that's a lot.

00:01:15.067 --> 00:01:17.033
You're gonna get overwhelmed!"
I got nothing from these people.

00:01:17.033 --> 00:01:18.734
I got nothing.
-They told you nothing.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:21.467
And so they play it,
and then everyone loved it.

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.200
That's got to feel --
That's got to feel good.

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.367
-It felt great.
It was the hugest relief.

00:01:25.367 --> 00:01:27.767
'Cause like, the unofficial
tagline of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons"

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:30.467
is, "Dungeons &amp; Dragons:
No, no, wait, hear me out."

00:01:30.467 --> 00:01:33.534
-No, it is really good, yeah.
-And, like, this is it.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.434
We walked in, and it's like
bringing this movie to meet

00:01:35.434 --> 00:01:37.634
mom and dad, because
this is the judge and jury

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:38.934
of "Dungeons &amp; Dragons."

00:01:38.934 --> 00:01:40.801
And they all went,
"oh, my God, it doesn't suck!"

00:01:40.801 --> 00:01:43.067
And we're like, "Yes!"
-Yeah. Exactly.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.434
Congratulations.
-Thank you!

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:46.467
-That's lot of pressure.
-It's great.

00:01:46.467 --> 00:01:48.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.067 --> 00:01:52.834
-But it's not your first turn
in a fantasy movie.

00:01:52.834 --> 00:01:56.501
Of course -- Yeah.
Let me jog your memory.

00:01:56.501 --> 00:01:59.834
Of course, we all remember you
from "Harry Potter."

00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:01.901
-Oh, yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:04.734
-Yeah, you were -- There's
a thing online, they said,

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.634
"Oh, my gosh, Rege-Jean Page
is a background actor

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.834
in 'Harry Potter.'"

00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.534
Is it seven maybe?
-Maybe.

00:02:11.534 --> 00:02:14.000
-Yeah, maybe.
-You're telling...

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.434
-Well, you know what? Let's just
show a clip, 'cause we have one.

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:17.868
Here we go.

00:02:17.868 --> 00:02:19.667
♪♪

00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:21.567
-They are coming.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:24.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:26.133
-That's the scene.

00:02:26.133 --> 00:02:27.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:35.701
♪♪

00:02:35.701 --> 00:02:38.434
Did you enjoy doing that?
-Yeah, no, hugely.

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.267
I mean, the best thing
about, like, background acting,

00:02:40.267 --> 00:02:42.000
particularly on big movies
like that --

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.968
and I recommend it
to every actor out there --

00:02:43.968 --> 00:02:45.734
is, essentially, no one
pays attention to you

00:02:45.734 --> 00:02:47.934
in the background,
so you get to be best actor spy.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.067
I was just watching, like,

00:02:49.067 --> 00:02:50.901
how these directors work
with these actors,

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:53.133
where Emma Watson hides
her phones between takes.

00:02:53.133 --> 00:02:55.400
Like, it was just --
And this is the valuable stuff.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.801
It was under the tablecloths
at the wedding, by the way.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.634
-That's where they do it. Wow.
-Sorry, Emma.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.801
-Yeah. Can we talk about
"The Gray Man"?

00:03:01.801 --> 00:03:03.634
-Yeah, all day long.

00:03:03.634 --> 00:03:06.000
-This is an action movie,
and it is action-packed.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.033
It is fantastic.
It's a lot of action.

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.501
-Yeah, it's huge.
-Yeah, and this is

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.000
the Russo brothers,
who are known for their

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.767
huge Marvel films.

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:14.200
-I mean, just a couple
little indie films.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:15.534
-Yeah. The biggest movies
in the world.

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.267
-The highest-grossing movies
pretty much of all time.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:18.734
-Yeah. How did you connect
with those guys?

00:03:18.734 --> 00:03:20.367
How did they hook up with you?

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.000
-I mean, there's different
versions of this story.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.100
So, like, there's a version that
Joe tells where his wife watched

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.367
"Bridgerton," there's a
version where he watched
it with his wife.

00:03:26.367 --> 00:03:28.834
There's a version where Anthony
says he was, like, at --

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.133
picking up his kids, and all
the mums were talking about me.

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:33.300
And he was like, "I need
to know who this dude is."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.934
-Yeah.
-I mean, the common thread is,

00:03:34.934 --> 00:03:37.300
essentially, some powerful men
had the women in their lives

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.634
talk to them, and we all know
who run the world at this point.

00:03:39.634 --> 00:03:41.367
-Yeah, yeah, we know
who runs the world.

00:03:41.367 --> 00:03:42.968
Exactly. That's correct.
-I think we do.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:46.033
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:03:46.033 --> 00:03:48.567
So you get to work with these
guys, and you go -- This is --

00:03:48.567 --> 00:03:51.367
I mean, the whole film
is a giant, giant fun film.

00:03:51.367 --> 00:03:54.434
Ryan Gosling.
You got Chris Evans.

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.901
-Mm-hmm.
Incredible and hilarious.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.100
-He is a great guy.
He's just a fun --

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.534
-Gosling's got the most
wonderful, wry, absurdist humor.

00:04:02.534 --> 00:04:05.334
And I think that Evans is very
kind of begrudgingly grateful.

00:04:05.334 --> 00:04:07.467
Because I think the --
the "trash 'stache" thing,
that's a Gosling original.

00:04:07.467 --> 00:04:10.167
He was just, like, throwing out
disses to Evans between takes.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.234
It was just like,
"It looks like a trash 'stache."

00:04:12.234 --> 00:04:13.834
Like, "You hit like a..."

00:04:13.834 --> 00:04:15.167
Like, it was just, like,
Gosling lines.

00:04:15.167 --> 00:04:16.968
-Back and forth, yeah.
It started with Gosling.

00:04:16.968 --> 00:04:18.934
-There's a ton of those
on the cutting-room floor.

00:04:18.934 --> 00:04:20.901
-Who do you -- Can you tell
everyone who you play?

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:23.000
-I play a man called
Denny Carmichael.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.667
He is the deliciously
devious head of the CIA.

00:04:25.667 --> 00:04:27.701
Here's the CliffsNotes.

00:04:27.701 --> 00:04:29.133
Essentially,
I'm Ryan and Chris' boss,

00:04:29.133 --> 00:04:30.801
I tell them to go out across
the world and punch each other

00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:32.234
in the face, and they do.
-There you go.

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:34.267
That's a great way
to sum up the film.

00:04:34.267 --> 00:04:35.767
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:38.367
Here's Rege-Jean Page
in "The Gray Man."

00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:39.801
Take a look at this.

00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:41.133
-Six.

00:04:41.133 --> 00:04:42.868
-Want to explain
whatever that was?

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.300
-Gun jammed.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.534
-That doesn't qualify
as an explanation.

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.200
-Maybe on a secure line.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:51.167
-I need a status report.
Insecure line.

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.467
Did the target say
anything to you?

00:04:53.467 --> 00:04:57.367
-Well, he was dead,
so, you know, no.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.934
-What about pocket litter?

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.501
Did you get anything
off his body?

00:05:04.067 --> 00:05:10.000
Six, did he have anything
on his person that you now have

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:13.400
that you'd like to give to me?

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.667
-Who was he?

00:05:15.667 --> 00:05:17.033
-A bad guy.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:20.634
-Yeah!
He's a bad guy. Watch out.

00:05:20.634 --> 00:05:22.534
Rege-Jean Page!

00:05:22.534 --> 00:05:25.133
"The Gray Man" is streaming
right now on Netflix.

